## Context

The project's committed `tickets/erg` (8 MB, built 2026-05-13) has
drifted from the current git-erg version and from IDH tooling:

- `~/.claude/scripts/refresh-STATE.py` fails against it ("Unknown
  command: list") — STATE Status regeneration is broken.
- The updated spec (global `tickets/AGENTS.md`, 2026-06-03) uses
  `Label:` headers and an `erg spec` command; this corpus uses `Tag:`
  (+ `tickets/.ergrc [tags]`). `erg migrate` exists for legacy files.
- IDH's own erg is a different build (2.3 MB) — two versions in play.

## Critical ordering constraint

**Binary + corpus + `.ergrc` must land in ONE PR.** The pre-commit hook
runs `erg validate`; if the binary and the ~390 ticket files (open +
closed) update in separate commits, the hook wedges in between. Run
`erg migrate` with the NEW binary, validate the whole corpus with the
NEW binary, commit everything together.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/erg` — committed bootstrap binary (project has NO
  `tickets/tools/go/` source; decide: copy a git-erg release binary vs
  vendor the source — check IDH / git-erg repo for the canonical
  distribution)
- `tickets/*.erg`, `tickets/closed/*.erg` — corpus to migrate (~390)
- `tickets/.ergrc` — `[tags]` section may rename with Tag->Label
- `scripts/check_ticket_structure.py` — project CI lint; may assume the
  old format
- `.claude/skills/ticket-*` (project) + IDH skills `pick-ticket`,
  `housekeeping`, `celebrate` — parse `erg ready --json` fields,
  `erg archive`, `erg close` output

## Actions

1. Obtain the current erg binary (or source); note its version in the
   PR body.
2. On a branch: replace `tickets/erg`, run `erg migrate` over the
   corpus, adapt `.ergrc`, run `erg check tickets/` until PASS.
3. Re-test integration points with the new binary:
   - `refresh-STATE.py` (the currently-broken `list` call)
   - `pick-ticket` / `housekeeping` flows: `ready --json` field names,
     `next-id`, `close`, `archive`
   - `scripts/check_ticket_structure.py` and the pre-commit hook
   - quickpr-style in-place close (Closed: header inference)
4. Re-triage against the new version's changelog/behaviour — possible
   free closures:
   - 0404: claim-detection substring false-positive (date-stamped
     branches claim 0260/0604) — fixed upstream?
   - 0391: atomic close+archive — now native?
   - 0388 / 0390: closed-in-open-dir guard, duplicate-ID guard — now
     native checks of `erg check`?
   Close any that the new version satisfies, with evidence in the log.
5. Update `.claude/CLAUDE.md` git-erg section / `tickets/AGENTS.md`
   pointer if commands or build instructions changed.

## Test

Red step before the swap: `tickets/erg list tickets/` (or the command
refresh-STATE.py uses) errors with "Unknown command". Green after: it
succeeds AND `erg check tickets/` passes on the migrated corpus AND
`pytest -m adherence` stays green.

## Verification

- [ ] `erg check tickets/` PASS with the new binary on the migrated corpus
- [ ] `refresh-STATE.py` runs end-to-end (Status block regenerates)
- [ ] pick-ticket / housekeeping / celebrate flows exercised once each
- [ ] CI green (pre-commit validate + check_ticket_structure)
- [ ] 0404/0391/0388/0390 re-triaged with evidence

## Invariants

- No ticket CONTENT changes — format/header migration only; log lines
  append-only
- `tickets/closed/` stays archived; no resurrection of closed tickets
- One PR, atomic

## Exit criteria

- New erg binary committed; corpus validates with it; the four
  integration surfaces work; re-triage logged on the four candidate
  tickets
